# Build context for the MIKE app image (see Dockerfile, compose.yaml).
#
# Two rules drive this file:
#   1. The image is BUILT from source here — anything the tree already holds as a build
#      output (frontend/dist, the mike and sandbox-bridge binaries, node_modules) is
#      either rebuilt in a stage or would silently ship stale bytes.
#   2. data/ holds kanban.db (encrypted secrets, session hashes) and data/tls/ (the local
#      CA private key). It is 0700 for a reason and must never become an image layer that
#      gets pushed and read by someone else.

# ── Secrets and runtime state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/
.env
*.trace
*.trace.old

# ── VCS / local working state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.worktrees
worktrees
extensions/
prompts/skills/
TODO.md
docs/
test-results
test-results2
frontend/test-results
frontend/test-results-json

# ── Rebuilt inside the image ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
# The Go stage gets this from the web stage, not the context: a context copy would be whatever the
# last local `npm run build` left behind.
frontend/dist
mike
# The committed bridge artifact is deliberately excluded: the image builds it from
# ./pkg/bridge/agent so a sandbox can never run an older bridge than this tree's source.
# `make bridge-check` remains the gate for the committed copy.
sandbox/sandbox-bridge
sandbox/sandbox-bridge.srcs

# ── Not needed by either build stage ─────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__
LICENSE
NOTICE
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
README.md
AGENTS.md
Makefile
compose.yaml
frontend/playwright.config.ts
frontend/vitest.config.ts
frontend/tests
